    dcterms:description "Dominant/codominant overstorey species are defined as species that dominate the tallest stratum with a canopy cover >5%.  If there are no layers that have a canopy cover >5% then the dominant/codominant overstorey species are defined as species that dominate the tallest layer which has the maximum recorded cover/abundance. " ;
